course: dictionary
lesson: 11406
title: Accountability: owning what you do
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accountability is a long word, but its main idea is simple. When you do something, you are responsible for it. «She took accountability for breaking the window and told the teacher the truth.» She did not hide it or blame someone else. That is accountability.
explain: Accountability is a noun, and it often goes with «for», as in accountability for a mistake. You can also say «hold someone to account», which means making them explain what they did. Clue words near it, such as explain, responsible or blame, often show what it means.
explain: The same idea applies to adults. «The head teacher must explain her decisions to parents and inspectors.» She answers to others for her choices. This kind of accountability keeps leaders fair, because people can ask them to explain.
fact: Accountability means being responsible for what you do.
fact: Accountability also means being ready to explain your actions and accept the results.
fact: «Taking accountability for a mistake» means owning up to it.
fact: In government and work, people in charge must explain their decisions and can be held to blame.
fact: Useful phrases: «take accountability», «hold someone to account», «accountability for».
exercise: «Mia broke the cup, so she told Mum the truth and offered to help pay for a new one.» What does Mia show? | Surprise | Anger | Boredom | *Accountability
exercise: Which phrase means making someone explain what they did? | Praise someone loudly | *Hold someone to account | Ignore someone | Forget someone
exercise: Which word means being responsible for your actions and ready to explain them? | Curiosity | Nervousness | Generosity | *Accountability
test: «The mayor had to explain why the bridge was closed to the town.» What does this show about the mayor? | *Accountability for her decision | Bravery | Accountability | Tiredness
test: What does «accountability for» usually go with? | *A mistake or action | A sunny day | A colour | A song
exam: Which sentence uses accountability correctly? | *The team took accountability for losing and planned to train harder. | The sky had accountability and was blue. | Accountability is a green colour. | We ate accountability for lunch.
